content.text:
Now run the tests for this file, plus typecheck/build.

Note: `screen.queryByRole` after `closed.unmount()` — testing-library's `screen` queries document.body; unmount clears that render. Sequential renders within one `it` accumulate in body unless auto-cleanup runs (vitest globals config? RTL auto-cleanup requires `globals: true` or explicit cleanup). Safer: use container-scoped queries instead of `screen`, or render both into separate containers and query each container. Let me simplify: query within containers.

Also the existing tests use `screen.getByRole('button', { name: /cancel/ })` — that works if auto-cleanup is on. Let me check the vitest setup for RTL cleanup. If `globals: true` in vitest config and RTL's auto-cleanup is imported via setup file (`@testing-library/jest-dom` doesn't do cleanup; `@testing-library/react` does auto-cleanup when globals are available). Since other test files render multiple times in one file and use `screen`, auto-cleanup is likely working (between tests, not within).

But my second test renders twice WITHIN one `it` and uses `screen` — the first render's DOM is removed by unmount(), so `screen.queryByRole` after unmount only sees the second render. That's fine: unmount removes nodes. But careful: after `closed.unmount()`, body has the second render's content only. OK.

Actually, to be safe and clearer, let me restructure that test to use containers.

Let me rewrite test 2:
```tsx
  it('不渲染「查看」按钮（选中态也不出现）', () => {
    const e = bgTaskEntry({ id: 'bg1' })
    const closed = render(<BgTaskEntry e={e} chrome={makeChrome(e, vi.fn())} />)
    const selected = render(
      <BgTaskEntry e={e} chrome={makeChrome(e, vi.fn(), vi.fn(), vi.fn(), true)} />,
    )
    for (const { container } of [closed, selected]) {
      expect(
        [...container.querySelectorAll('button')].some((b) => /查看/.test(b.textContent ?? '')),
      ).toBe(false)
    }
  })
```
Cleaner, no unmount ordering concerns. Let me apply.

